join Lucretia leftmost
Lucretia: Man, if it wasn’t for the whole eldritch-zombies and split-consciousness thing, having these powers would be awesome.  Feels good not needing to rely on anyone! #id:39
join Syn_Lucretia rightmost
Syn_Lucretia: Yeah, yeah, it must be nice not being held hostage in an alternate universe. We get it. Anyways, look at what I found! #id:3a
Lucretia: Is that cthulhu? #id:3b
Syn_Lucretia: Well, obviously no, but it kinda looks like him. They call it an “Old One” in the painting. They seem to be worshipped like gods? And look in the corner– #id:3c
Lucretia: Argus. #id:3d
Syn_Lucretia: Right, but he’s not mentioned anywhere. And given how nearly everything’s covered up or destroyed, I’m guessing this was stuff he didn’t want anyone to see. #id:3e
Lucretia: So what does it all mean? #id:3f
Syn_Lucretia: I’m not sure. But maybe Argus has been causing chaos for longer than we realize. #id:40
Lucretia: I’m starting to worry this will be a lot harder than just getting him to undo the deal. #id:41
Syn_Lucretia: Depends how badly we care about saving the world. #id:42